WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:01.567
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.267
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.434
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.300
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.634
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.501
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:09.434
Well, guys,
tonight was the drawing

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:12.901
for the $1.3 billion
Mega Millions jackpot,

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:15.234
the second largest in history.

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:17.300
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Whoa.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.300
-The odds of winning
were one in 302 million.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:22.467
But I have a system.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.100
I buy two tickets.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.167
[ Laughter and applause ]
[ Cluck ]

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.501
Everyone always says that
they'll be smart with the money

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.167
and then they spend
the next three hours scrolling

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.501
through photos
of lawn fountains.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.634
[ Laughter ]
Like, "Hey, found one."

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:35.100
But the lottery can be fun,

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.701
especially before the drawing,
when people say to their boss,

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:40.000
"Quick heads up -- you might get
a profanity-laced phone call

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.234
from me tonight.
Talk to you later.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:45.734
That's right, but today is
Friday the 13th.
-Whoa.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.501
[ Cheering, oohs,
and applause ]

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.033
People say it's unlucky.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.634
Meanwhile, everyone who flew
Southwest over the holidays

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.634
was like, "Last month
wasn't so lucky,

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.901
[ Laughter and applause ]
either."

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.601
That's right,
today is Friday the 13th.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:58.868
-Careful.
Careful there, Jimmy.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.300
It's not over yet.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.267
-Well, actually, I had
a great Friday the 13th.

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:04.167
It's Hot Dog Friday here at NBC.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:06.634
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:08.334
I'm going to save this
for later.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.234
[ Laughter ]
[ Bloop! ]

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:11.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.234
Don't forget the bun, hon.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:13.934
[ Bloop! ]

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:16.067
[ Clapping ]
Cool!

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.367
-This is the best
Friday the 13th ever!

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:23.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Congratulations, bud!

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:25.501
[ Oohs ]

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:30.067
Well, get this --
I saw that tomorrow,

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.234
the Rockefeller Center
Christmas Tree comes down.

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:34.801
[ Awws and applause ]
And --

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:39.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.434
-Ooh!
-And hold on to your
ticket stubs

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.868
because one lucky audience
member will be taking it home.

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:44.801
That's right.

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:47.200
[ Oohs, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.067
People always ask,
"What happens to the tree?"

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.000
Well, it's actually shipped
to a paper mill,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.067
where it becomes thousands

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:53.567
of mishandled
classified documents.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.868
Yep, everyone's still talking
about the classified documents

00:01:57.868 --> 00:02:00.434
that were found
in President Biden's garage.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.300
[ Laughter ]
Even worse, it came out

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.634
that his neighbor asked
to borrow one

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:04.934
and still hasn't returned it.

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:06.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:07.701
But it might help
explain things.

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.834
According to a new report,
Biden's last few days

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.501
as vice president were chaotic

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:14.634
and boxes were being packed
until the last minute.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.667
Biden was like, "That's it,
I'm changing my review

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.234
on College Hunks Hauling Junk.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:19.868
[ Laughter ]
Losers."

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:23.267
Of course,
Democrats are concerned

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:27.033
this scandal could weaken Biden
as a candidate in 2024,

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:28.501
as opposed to their
previous concern,

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:31.267
that the ravages of time
would weaken him by 2024.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:33.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.767
Imagine losing the most
powerful job on Earth

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:37.667
because you kept putting off
cleaning out the garage.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.200
Some more political news --
it seems like every day

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.634
we're learning more
about George Santos

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:46.467
and I actually saw a clip
from back in October,

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:49.767
where he and his opponent were
asked the same question, okay?

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:51.000
And I'm surprised nobody
noticed this.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:51.934
Take a look.
This is real.

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.634
-So, Mr. Zimmerman, name one

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:55.767
of your favorite
family traditions.

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:58.334
-Oh, my nephews and I,
my brother, and sister-in-law

00:02:58.334 --> 00:02:59.634
get together in our sweats

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.734
and eat the food that we
shouldn't eat all year round.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.901
It goes into -- Haagen-Dazs
is always a staple.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:06.400
-Mr. Santos, your favorite
family tradition.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.000
-Every moment
we can get together

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.701
that's kind of a down time,

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:10.868
it's sweatpants,

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:12.868
pints of Haagen-Dazs all
over the place.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:15.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.701
-What?

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:18.567
-That's for real.
-What?!

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:20.400
-That's for real.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.467
-I've never seen identity theft
happen in real time.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:26.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:27.834
"That's my favorite moment.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.801
That's weird."

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:31.100
Then he said,
"I'm Marcia Kramer,

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.100
host of 'The Point.'

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.100
Thanks for watching.
Good night."

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.834
[ Laughter ]
And you go, "Wait."

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.501
Is that bizarre?
-My God.

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.767
-Switching gears --
I heard that ABC is planning

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.868
a new series called
"Jeopardy! Masters,"

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:42.634
where the highest-ranked
"Jeopardy!" contestants

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:45.501
will face off to win the title
of Jeopardy! Masters Champion.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:46.934
[ Oohs ]
Yeah. And, while we don't know

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:48.234
much more about the show,

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:50.434
we do know that these
contestants missed the cut.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:56.934
-Sam.
-What is Jamaica?

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.434
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.200
-What's a raccoon?
-No.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.100
-What is seven?
-No.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:12.634
-Ray.
-Who are the Beastie Boys?

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:13.901
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:19.267
-What is a beaver?
-No.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:26.534
-Who's Ed Asner?
-No.

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:27.267
[ Laughter ]
And finishing off...

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:31.934
-Who is Shrek?
-No.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.501
[ Laughter ]
-Oh! Unfortunate.
That's tough.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:36.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:37.734
-That was good stuff.
-"What is a beaver?"

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:38.834
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:42.334
-You guys -- Hey, guys,
everyone's excited about this --

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:45.667
the NFL playoffs kick off
tomorrow and --

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:47.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.901
The NFL.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:50.634
And this is incredible --

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:51.601
Tom Brady is going

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:53.067
for his eighth Super Bowl.

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:54.734
[ Oohs ]
Yeah. When he heard,

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:56.901
George Santos was like,
"He's only one behind me."

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.434 --> 00:05:00.167
Meanwhile, for the first time
in six years,

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:02.000
the New York Giants
made the playoffs.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:07.534
Then the Jets were like,

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:09.100
"Just say New York is
in the playoffs, okay?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.868
[ Laughter ]
Why do you have to be
so specific?"

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:11.801
That's right,
there will be a ton

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:13.100
of great games this weekend.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.534
Tomorrow night, you can watch
the Jacksonville Jaguars

00:05:15.534 --> 00:05:18.501
take on the Los Angeles Chargers
right here on NBC.

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:21.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
The game is two of the league's
best young quarterbacks,

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.667
Trevor Lawrence
and Justin Herbert.

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:23.968
Can we see them?

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.033
Yeah, there they are.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.100
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.534
Well, today,
Trevor Lawrence said...

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:31.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.167
And Justin Herbert said...

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:35.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.367
Then Brenden Schooler,
from the Patriots, said...

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:43.334
Then Andrew Van Ginkel,
from the Dolphins, said...

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:48.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:49.901
Tanner Muse, from the Seahawks,
said...

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:53.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:55.734
Then George Kittle,
from the 49ers, said...

00:05:57.934 --> 00:06:00.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:02.267
Then Billy Price,
from the Cardinal, said...

00:06:03.834 --> 00:06:08.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.234
[ Cheering ]
Finally --

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:14.434
Finally, Las Vegas Raiders
owner Mark Davis said...

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:18.734
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:19.434
[ Indistinct ]

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.934
Should be a good game.

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:23.934
Some entertainment news --
a new action movie,

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:26.133
called "Plane," opened today,

00:06:26.133 --> 00:06:28.167
[ Oohs ]
about a heroic pilot,
but I was a little surprised

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:30.267
that they couldn't think
of a better name than "Plane."

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:31.767
[ Laughter ]
But regardless,
judging by the trailer,

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.801
it looks great.
Check it out.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:36.000
-A determined pilot
will do anything

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.667
to rescue his passengers in the
pulse-pounding thriller...

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:41.234
...from the people
who brought you...

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:44.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:53.067
Wow. That looks good.
I like that.

00:06:53.067 --> 00:06:56.000
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:00.334
Well, listen to this --
I saw a new study that found

00:07:00.334 --> 00:07:03.501
that sitting too much
is hazardous to your health.

00:07:03.501 --> 00:07:05.734
Yeah, that explains why I feel
so healthy eating Domino's

00:07:05.734 --> 00:07:07.133
while standing
over the kitchen sink.

00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:09.334
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:12.534
And, finally, this is --
this is actually real footage.

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:13.968
What I'm going to show you is --
-This is real.

00:07:13.968 --> 00:07:16.167
-This one is real, yeah.
This is not a joke.

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:18.734
But this security footage
caught this moment.

00:07:18.734 --> 00:07:21.234
A man in Brazil
was closing up his shop

00:07:21.234 --> 00:07:23.501
with his father-in-law, okay?

00:07:23.501 --> 00:07:25.300
And, well, just watch this
and enjoy it.

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:28.501
-[ Whistling ]

00:07:28.501 --> 00:07:29.934
[ Squeak ]

00:07:29.934 --> 00:07:31.334
[ Whistling ]
[ Audience gasping ]

00:07:31.334 --> 00:07:32.501
[ Clanging ]
[ Ohhs ]

00:07:32.501 --> 00:07:33.901
-[ Crying out
in foreign language ]

00:07:33.901 --> 00:07:34.701
-[ Speaking
foreign language ]

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.567 --> 00:07:40.667
[ Ohhs ]
-[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:07:42.534 --> 00:07:44.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.667 --> 00:07:45.567
[ Gasping ]

00:07:45.567 --> 00:07:46.567
[ Clang ]

00:07:46.567 --> 00:07:48.667
[ Ohhs, laughter,
and applause ]

00:07:52.534 --> 00:07:54.367
[ Rimshot ]
-Wow.

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:55.400
-Come on.
-That --

00:07:57.767 --> 00:07:59.634
That happened seven more times.

00:07:59.634 --> 00:08:01.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.033 --> 00:08:02.667
His father was all --
His father-in-law's like,

00:08:02.667 --> 00:08:03.834
"Wait, I don't remember that."

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:05.934
[ Laughter ]
Then the father-in-law's like,

00:08:05.934 --> 00:08:07.834
"Let me recover for a moment
by lying on the ground

00:08:07.834 --> 00:08:09.033
with my legs spread wide."

00:08:09.033 --> 00:08:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.701 --> 00:08:11.033
Hey, guys.

00:08:11.033 --> 00:08:12.767
[ Cheering and applause ]
Once again, just a reminder --

00:08:12.767 --> 00:08:15.767
this weekend is
NFL Super Wild Card Weekend

00:08:15.767 --> 00:08:17.834
and NBC has two big games...
-Whoa!

00:08:17.834 --> 00:08:20.601
-...the Chargers versus
the Jaguars on Saturday night;

00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:23.267
then Sunday night, it's the
Ravens versus the Bengals.

00:08:23.267 --> 00:08:25.434
So, just stay right here
on NBC all weekend.

00:08:25.434 --> 00:08:26.501
It's going to be good!

00:08:26.501 --> 00:08:28.167
[ Cheering and applause ]
We appreciate it.

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:30.334
But first, what a show
we have for you tonight.

00:08:30.334 --> 00:08:32.801
She is starring
in the Broadway revival

00:08:32.801 --> 00:08:35.133
of "Funny Girl,"
which is playing now

00:08:35.133 --> 00:08:37.634
at the August Wilson Theatre.

00:08:37.634 --> 00:08:39.467
Lea Michelle is here tonight!

00:08:39.467 --> 00:08:41.334
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:08:41.334 --> 00:08:43.300
-Wow.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:46.000
-Plus, you know her as Max
from "Stranger Things."

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.367
You can also see her
in the new movie "The Whale,"

00:08:48.367 --> 00:08:49.501
which is in theaters now.

00:08:49.501 --> 00:08:51.200
Sadie Sink is here!

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.367
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Drumming ]

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:56.300
And we got music from Dayglow!

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:00.334
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:09:00.334 --> 00:09:02.067
Well, guys, today is Friday
and that's usually

00:09:02.067 --> 00:09:03.701
when I catch up
with some personal stuff.

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:05.501
I check my inbox, return emails,

00:09:05.501 --> 00:09:06.968
and I write out
some thank you notes

00:09:06.968 --> 00:09:08.400
and I was wondering
if I could write some tonight.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.367
[ Cheering and applause ]
Is that okay?

00:09:10.367 --> 00:09:12.534
James, can I get some thank you
note-writing music please?

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:13.901
[ Playing tender tune ]

00:09:13.901 --> 00:09:16.434
[ Laughter ]
[ Clears throat ]

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:18.267
-Jeez!
-He's in a good mood.

00:09:18.267 --> 00:09:19.367
-Wow.

00:09:19.367 --> 00:09:20.467
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.801 --> 00:09:24.133
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:09:24.133 --> 00:09:25.834
Thank you, "Plane,"

00:09:25.834 --> 00:09:28.400
for being in the one flight this
week that didn't get canceled.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:31.634 --> 00:09:32.300
Appreciate it.

00:09:34.734 --> 00:09:36.000
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.734
Thank you,
Dr Pepper-flavored Peeps,

00:09:39.734 --> 00:09:42.100
for, somehow, not being called
Dr Peepers.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.334
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Why not?

00:09:43.334 --> 00:09:44.467
-It's right there.

00:09:44.467 --> 00:09:45.234
-Why wouldn't you do it?
-Why would you not?

00:09:45.234 --> 00:09:46.801
-What?

00:09:46.801 --> 00:09:49.067
At least Dr. Pibb.
-Call me. These people have
to call me.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.634
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:09:51.634 --> 00:09:54.567
Thank you, people with Christmas
decorations still up...

00:09:54.567 --> 00:09:56.801
[ Laughter ]
for introducing your neighbors

00:09:56.801 --> 00:09:59.334
to the fun new game
Lazy, Out of Town, or Dead?

00:09:59.334 --> 00:10:02.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:02.934 --> 00:10:04.300
Not necessarily healthy.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:06.067
[ Laughter ]

00:10:06.067 --> 00:10:07.334
♪♪
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:10:07.334 --> 00:10:10.000
Thank you, gas stoves,
for looking like

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.400
I'm staring down
at a Troll doll drum circle.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:15.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:20.133 --> 00:10:21.334
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.334 --> 00:10:23.434
Thank you,
Fruit by the Foot,

00:10:23.434 --> 00:10:25.367
for being the red carpet
of fruit leather.

00:10:25.367 --> 00:10:28.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:32.067 --> 00:10:34.300
Thank you, Scratch-Off
lottery tickets,

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.234
for pretty much being the only
reason people still use coins.

00:10:37.234 --> 00:10:39.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:39.767 --> 00:10:40.434
Hey, that's interesting.

00:10:40.434 --> 00:10:41.234
-[ Indistinct ]

00:10:45.334 --> 00:10:46.634
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:10:46.634 --> 00:10:50.067
Thank you, today,
for being Friday the 13th,

00:10:50.067 --> 00:10:52.067
which means only one thing...

00:10:52.067 --> 00:10:55.167
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.701
It's Patrick Dempsey's birthday!

00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:03.334
[ Hip hop oompah music plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:03.334 --> 00:11:06.200
[ Clapping rhythmically ]

00:11:13.167 --> 00:11:14.234
There you have it!

00:11:14.234 --> 00:11:15.501
Those were my Thank You Notes.

00:11:15.501 --> 00:11:16.834
When we come back,
we're playing Charades

00:11:16.834 --> 00:11:18.634
